THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
--------------------

Portions of this release are derived from the GNU ISO C++ Library
(libstdc++), part of the GNU Compiler Collection:

    Copyright (C) 1997-2026 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1

Date/time portions are also derived from the GNU C Library (glibc):

    Copyright (C) 1991-2026 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later

The files listed below contain code, comments, test data, algorithms
and/or identifier naming taken or adapted from those projects --
principally libstdc++ <bits/locale_facets.tcc>,
<bits/locale_facets_nonio.tcc> and config/locale/gnu/monetary_members.cc,
and glibc's time/ and locale/ sources:

  IOv2/facet/numeric.h
      The num_get / num_put implementation: the two-stage formatting
      structure ("Stage 1 / Stage 2"), the boolalpha longest-match
      extraction loop, integer and floating-point field extraction,
      decimal-part grouping, and the accompanying
      "_GLIBCXX_RESOLVE_LIB_DEFECTS" / LWG defect-resolution comments.

  IOv2/facet/facet_helper.h
      add_grouping()    -- adapted from libstdc++ __add_grouping()
      verify_grouping() -- adapted from libstdc++ __verify_grouping(),
                           including its explanatory comments.

  IOv2/facet/monetary.h
      The money_get / money_put implementation and its internal parse
      state (testvalid, testdecfound, sign_size, last_pos).

  IOv2/facet/monetary_details.h
      s_construct_pattern() -- adapted from libstdc++
      _S_construct_pattern() in config/locale/gnu/monetary_members.cc,
      retaining its parameter names and explanatory comments.

  IOv2/facet/timeio.h
      extract_num()      -- adapted from libstdc++ time_get's
                            _M_extract_num().
      day_of_the_week(), isleap() and the month/year-day table --
      adapted from glibc's time sources, together with roughly ten of
      glibc's comments carried over verbatim.

  IOv2/facet/timeio_details.h
      The parsing of the era records that glibc exposes through
      nl_langinfo(_NL_TIME_ERA_ENTRIES) -- adapted from glibc's
      time/era.c.

  IOv2/cvt/code_cvt.h
      The UTF-8 decoding bias constants (0x3080, 0xE2080, 0x3C82080).

  IOv2Test/**
      Test fixtures, inputs and expected-value tables adapted from the
      libstdc++ testsuite.  Several of these files cite the upstream
      test they came from in their own comments.

